<p>Renting a car at the airport makes sense if you're planning to explore the wider Catalonia region, but for a stay confined to Barcelona itself it usually creates more problems than it solves — the historic centre has restricted traffic zones, limited and expensive parking, and a layout that rewards walking and public transport over driving.</p>

